iding  reassurance and that's what we'll be  doing but just reading into how you put  that obviously very diplomatic about the  numbers but you would always like more  people presumably therefore not fewer as  is the prediction as I say from the  mayor are you at rock bottom now around  about the 30,000 level an awful lot of  things can happen I can't predict what  will happen with our funding it's my job  to make an evidence-based case I did  that in the autumn we have another  hundred and twelve million which we are  now going to be investing in the fight  against knife crime it's my job to look  at what the evidence is and to argue for  more and I will be doing that if I feel  that we cannot get on top of this  problem in commissioner can you make a  prediction that in another years time  you'll be able to to sit in front of the  cameras and and tell us that we are  getting on top of this issue if we take  the example of scooter enabled crime  that had been going up like this in the  two years before I arrived three months  in to my commissioner ship we start in a  whole range of new tactics and we put  even more effort into that and you'll be  aware that's quite a fair amount of that  involves robbery and sometimes in  knives and weapons as well that is now  coming right down I want to see the same  with knife crime I hope we will see the  same with knife crime I do not believe  the police can do that by themselves and  I need others to get involved and I need  the public to help us  and lastly commissioner a question about  not only subject question about  Salisbury because of course the  Metropolitan Police in charge of the  investigation into what happened to the  the screep house what can you tell us  about the state of that investigation  for instance have you even identified  any potential suspects yet so I'm not  gonna give you a an update on the  investigation I will leave that to the  investigation leads and and to Neel Basu  what I will say is it's a v